# This repo now serves server/install.sh straight from raw.githubusercontent.com
# into `bash` on a Linux server. Windows line endings there would break in a way
# that is hard to read: bash treats the carriage return as part of the command
# and reports "command not found: git\r". Force LF so an edit made on Windows
# can never ship that.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
# The two Windows launchers in tools/ are the one exception. cmd.exe reads a .cmd file
# with Unix line endings most of the time, and "most of the time" is not what a reader
# should get from the one command a chapter asks them to type.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
